                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I read the reviews that the controls were broken. I expected to be in pain but I didn't expect this much pain. It's just... unplayable on Steam Deck. I played Nights of Azure 2 on Switch with horrendous framerate but otherwise no issues but for Nights of Azure 1 on Steam... the controls are so painful, nothing makes sense, not even with custom community layouts.\n\nThere is no way to play this game with a controller. And it is supposed to be a console game, it released on PS3, PS4 and Vita as well as PC.\n\nIt's a horrendous experience. Absolutely awful.\n\nI knew the game was going to be trashy and grindy, I played and finished the sequel after all, I knew what I was getting into, but I didn't expect to suffer this much with the original anyway.",
